\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textcolor {blue}{\textbf  {[L1 Software]}}/\textcolor {teal}{\textbf  {[L2 Bit-True]}}\ Controlled In-Sample Stress Benchmark on Subject 1 across all five standardized PhysioNet FECGSYNDB stress test cases (TC1--TC5, 75,000 samples each). Evaluated at $\pm 50\,$ms tolerance window across 35 benchmark evaluations. Methods are ordered consistently across all test cases. Note: Under TC1--TC3 on Lead 27, single-channel Template Subtraction (Fixed) and Hankel-SVD V1 yield identical beat counts (546 TP, 168 FP, 170 FN in TC1) because both algorithms isolate identical dominant maternal QRS complexes, leaving identical residual noise profiles passed to the same downstream Peak-Energy detector. Deep U-Net (1-Ch) is evaluated in-sample on \texttt  {sub01}. Runtime is wall-clock time per 5-second window.}}{9}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
